  "merger_description": "Kinetic Holding Company Pty Ltd (Kinetic) proposes to acquire 100% of the shares in L.C. Dyson\u2019s Bus Services Pty Ltd (Dysons, together with its affiliates, the Dysons Group) pursuant to a share sale agreement.\n\nKinetic also proposes to acquire certain freehold and leasehold interests in bus depot assets currently leased by the Dysons Group and owned by related parties of Dysons\u2019 shareholders, namely 3D Management Properties Pty Ltd, 324 Gen Investments Pty Ltd, 3D Properties (Kyneton) Pty Ltd and 3D Properties (Wodonga) Pty Ltd. Kinetic is proposing to acquire the bus depot assets under separate Land Sale Contracts.\n\nThe share sale agreement and each of the Land Sale Contracts are interdependent, with simultaneous settlement and completion. Given the interdependencies between each of these agreements, Kinetic is notifying the proposed acquisitions together as a single notification for the purposes of s 51ABX(5) of the CCA (Proposed Transaction).\n\nKinetic is a transportation company that operates bus services in Australia and overseas. This is predominantly under the Kinetic brand but also (in Australia) in:  \n\n\u2022 the Northern Territory, Queensland and Western Australia under the Kinetic Specialised Resources brand;  \n\n\u2022 in Victoria, Sydney and Western Australia under the SkyBus brand; and  \n\n\u2022 in Queensland under the Koala Koaches brand and SkyBus brands.\n\nThese services include, depending on the region, urban route and school services, regional bus services, and charter bus services, airport transfers bus services and some specialised bus services, for example to the mining and resources sector.\n\nDysons is a family-owned coach and bus operator based in Melbourne. It provides services in Victoria, regional New South Wales and regional South Australia under the Dysons brand. These services include urban route services, school services, regional bus services, rail replacement services and charter services.",
